WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.133
-Welcome. Enjoy yourselves.
Welcome, everybody.

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:05.501
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.000
You're here.
You made it.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.501
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:12.834
Man, it was an exciting weekend
in -- in sports.

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:14.767
The Kentucky Derby.
Did you see this?

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:18.434
It's the second biggest upset
in the race's 148-year history.

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.801
It won --
80-1 was the long shot.

00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:23.133
Yeah. And it was named --
Rich Strike

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:24.467
was the name of the horse.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:26.767
Rich Strike, which sounds more
like your local anchor

00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:28.000
who does sports and weather.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:30.868
"And now with Rich Strike
with the weather."

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:32.067
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.434
Rich Strike sounds like
a pack of cigarettes

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:34.534
your grandma used to smoke.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:37.067
"Give me a pack
of Rich Strikes."

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:38.234
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:40.467
The horse's odds were 80-1.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.801
Yeah, that's like if today
I was talking

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:45.300
about President Bill de Blasio.
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.200
Can you -- do you understand
what that means?

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.467
Meanwhile, this weekend was also
Mother's Day, of course.

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:52.767
Happy Mother's Day
to all the mothers out there.

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:56.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:58.467
And I saw that First Lady
Jill Biden

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:02.000
spent the day in Ukraine and met
with the Ukrainian First Lady.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.300
Yeah. Basically, Joe got her
an edible arrangement

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:05.467
for Mother's Day and
Jill was like, "You know what?

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:08.300
I'm going to go to Ukraine.
I'm good."

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.834
And this was actually very cool.

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:12.234
At the request of
Ukrainian President Zelenskyy,

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:15.033
Bono and the Edge held
a surprise concert yesterday

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:17.267
at a subway station in Kyiv.

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:18.567
[ Audience oohs ]

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.567
That's amazing. That's --
it was the first time a guy

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.033
broke out a guitar
in a subway station

00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:23.434
and people actually cheered.

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:25.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:27.067
Let's switch gears.

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:29.100
As part of the investigation
against him,

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:31.901
Former President Trump has been
asked to turn over

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:34.300
four cell phones,
but he claims he can't

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.767
because he lost all of them.

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:38.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.801
Yeah, Trump said he doesn't know
where the phones are.

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:44.834
Then a minute later,

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:46.667
Eric Trump's stomach
started ringing.

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:48.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:51.567
[As Trump] "You --
you swallowed --"

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:53.667
[Normally] Well, get this.
A Sherpa in Nepal

00:01:53.667 --> 00:01:56.434
has set a new world record
after scaling Mount Everest

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.667
for the 26th time.

00:01:58.667 --> 00:01:59.834
[ Audience oohs ]

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:01.534
Yeah, so if you think
your friend who just ran

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:03.434
a half marathon is insufferable,

00:02:03.434 --> 00:02:04.767
try having lunch with this guy.

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:08.167
Yeah, the guy has his reasons.

00:02:08.167 --> 00:02:09.701
When asked what motivates him,
he said,

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:12.100
"I have AT&amp;T. It's the only
place I get service.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.200
I got to --"

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.434
Well, this isn't good --
A former sheriff's deputy

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:19.701
in Arizona has been arrested
for allegedly crashing weddings

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:22.701
and stealing thousands of
dollars' worth of wedding gifts.

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:24.267
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:24.267 --> 00:02:25.868
His friends got suspicious
when they saw

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:27.601
his kitchen had 11 air fryers.

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:29.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:32.267
Hey, I read that a 1,000-pound
great white shark

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:34.334
has been spotted near
the Jersey shore.

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:35.767
[ Audience oohs ]

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:38.467
Yeah, scientists tagged it with
a tracker a few years ago,

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:40.968
whereas the other sharks off
the coast of Jersey put it,

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:42.968
"He's wearing a wire.
He's wearing --"

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:44.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:47.067
Guys, before we go on,
I'd like to take a moment

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:49.234
to thank some of our sponsors
for the "Tonight Show."

00:02:49.234 --> 00:02:51.834
because they don't always fit in
the commercial breaks,

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:53.300
and we want to make sure
we mention all of them.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.534
So it's time for
the "Tonight Show" sponsors.

